# hermetic-consumption drives the validator under test over the real shipped corpus (arm C) and over
# mini distributions it seeds in mktemp from two shipped fixtures' run.sh and inputs.decl.
# reason: core/fixtures/ is declared whole because arm C scans every fixture directory's inputs.decl
# and run.sh and derives the scanned count itself by enumerating core/fixtures/*/; a narrower
# declaration would shrink the corpus and C would read a smaller clean line. It also covers lib/
# (the sourced preamble) and the two producer fixtures the worlds are seeded from.
# core-paths.sh is the mapper the validator resolves beside the corpus; VERSION is the marker both
# this run.sh and the validator walk up for.
!scripts/validate-hermetic-consumption.sh
core/scripts/core-paths.sh
core/fixtures/
VERSION
